  "addScreenPermissionSteps": "To read a QR code off your screen, your Mac needs to let Tanooki Auth take a picture of it. Tanooki Auth only looks when you press \"Scan my screen\", and the picture never leaves this Mac.\n\n1. Open System Settings (the gear icon in the Dock, or Apple menu > System Settings).\n2. Click \"Privacy & Security\" in the left column.\n3. Click \"Screen & System Audio Recording\".\n4. Turn on the switch next to Tanooki Auth. If it isn't in the list, click +, pick Tanooki Auth from Applications, and turn it on.\n5. Your Mac will ask to quit Tanooki Auth. Click \"Quit & Reopen\", then press \"Scan my screen\" again.",
