  "securityUiKitPaperButton": "Print paper backup",
  "securityUiSkipForNow": "Skip for now",
  "securityExtrasPrivacy": "No account, no tracking. Your setup keys are stored encrypted on this device. The app goes online only for: a clock check (it asks the Tanooki Auth server for the time, at most once an hour while codes are on screen and when you tap \"Codes not working?\"; nothing about you or your accounts is sent), breach alerts if you turn them on (downloads the public breach list), sync, phone link and emergency access if you set them up (they carry only encrypted data the server can't read), buying Premium, and feedback you choose to send (your message, your email if you type one, and the app version and device type if you leave that ticked; never your accounts, codes or anything else in the app). 2FA guides open in your web browser.",
